{
  // NOTE ON THIS FILE'S HISTORY, read before changing `main`/`assets` again:
  //
  // From this repo's extraction (`fc1c239`, 2026-07-20) through commit
  // `1985938`/`34166ac` (2026-09-05), `main` pointed at a SvelteKit build
  // output (`svelte/.svelte-kit/cloudflare/_worker.js`) that
  // `@sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare` compiled from `worker/svelte/` — a
  // status page (`+page.svelte`) plus a generic XRPC-to-MCP-router POST
  // proxy (`src/routes/xrpc/[...path]/+server.ts`). `assets.directory`
  // pointed at that build's static client output
  // (`./svelte/.svelte-kit/cloudflare/client`). `worker/src/app.ts` (with
  // `defence-handlers.ts`/`taxonomy.ts`/`classes-index.ts`) already
  // existed the whole time, already implemented this repo's actual
  // product — four XRPC GET routes under
  // `com.etzhayyim.apps.openCofog.*` (list/get COFOG divisions, groups,
  // classes) — and was already documented in the README as "the XRPC
  // router", but was NOT wired to `main`, so it was never actually served
  // by this Worker.
  //
  // Commit `34166ac` ("migrate open-cofog worker UI from svelte to cljs")
  // repointed `main` to `./src/app.ts` — for the first time actually
  // deploying this repo's real product — but did three things badly at
  // the same time: it deleted `worker/svelte/` (including `+server.ts`)
  // without preserving it anywhere; it did not build a `worker/cljs/`
  // replacement following this workspace's shadow-cljs+reagent+re-frame+
  // jp-go-dds convention (ADR-2608260900) at all; and it repointed
  // `assets.directory` at `../web/dist`, the output of an unrelated,
  // separately-scaffolded root-level app
  // (`src/cloud_itonami/open_cofog/{desktop,state,ui}.cljs`, built with
  // kotoba-ui/appkit, not jp-go-dds) that duplicates this same status
  // page outside `worker/`. It also left `APP_FRAMEWORK` stale
  // (`"sveltekit-edge-bff"`) even though SvelteKit was gone.
  //
  // THIS migration (frontend-only, scoped to `worker/svelte` →
  // `worker/cljs`) fixes the parts of that in its scope:
  //   - `assets.directory` → `./cljs/public` (this repo's own
  //     shadow-cljs+reagent+re-frame+jp-go-dds build, see `cljs/`).
  //   - `APP_FRAMEWORK` → `"cljs-reagent-re-frame-jp-go-dds"`.
  //   - `+server.ts` recovered from git history
  //     (`34166ac623dafdc7013013f7a49b9064c06ed8f4^1`) and preserved
  //     byte-identical (plus a header) at
  //     `worker/src/xrpc-mcp-router-proxy.ts` — see that file.
  //
  // `main` is DELIBERATELY NOT dropped and NOT repointed at the moved
  // proxy, unlike this workspace's usual "no source calls
  // env.ASSETS.fetch → drop main" default for a frontend-only migration.
  // `src/app.ts`/`defence-handlers.ts`/`taxonomy.ts`/`classes-index.ts`
  // were read and confirmed to contain no `ASSETS` reference — but unlike
  // a placeholder scaffold, `app.ts` is this repo's actual, independently
  // live product (confirmed against the README and its own 162 lines of
  // routing/data logic), and dropping `main` would take that service out
  // of the deploy path entirely, not just this status page. That would be
  // a strictly worse regression than leaving the pre-existing gap below
  // in place, so `main` stays `./src/app.ts` (those four files are also
  // out of scope for this frontend migration — see the migration task's
  // "Do NOT touch" list).
  //
  // CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: because `app.ts`'s `fetch` handles every
  // request itself and never calls `env.ASSETS.fetch(request)`,
  // `assets.directory` is still not wired to serve anything through this
  // Worker even after this fix — same as it was, unreachable, when it
  // pointed at `../web/dist`. That gap predates this migration (it dates
  // to `34166ac`'s `main` repoint, or arguably to the original
  // `fc1c239` extraction never wiring `app.ts` at all) and closing it
  // would require editing `worker/src/app.ts` to fall through to
  // `env.ASSETS.fetch` for unmatched paths, which is out of scope here.
  //
  // This whole edit is UNVERIFIED: `wrangler deploy`/`wrangler dev` were
  // not run against it.
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "etzhayyim-open-cofog",
  "main": "./src/app.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-04-20",
  "compatibility_flags": [
    "nodejs_compat"
  ],
  "account_id": "4da88288dc30d9ee257f319d3c33ecf0",
  "workers_dev": false,
  "routes": [
    {
      "pattern": "open-cofog.etzhayyim.com/*",
      "zone_name": "etzhayyim.com"
    }
  ],
  "vars": {
    "APP_HANDLE": "open-cofog.etzhayyim.com",
    "PRIMARY_DID": "did:web:open-cofog.etzhayyim.com",
    "APP_FRAMEWORK": "cljs-reagent-re-frame-jp-go-dds",
    "AGENTGATEWAY_MCP_ROUTER_URL": "https://mcp.etzhayyim.com/xrpc/com.etzhayyim.mcp.message"
  },
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./cljs/public",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash",
    "not_found_handling": "none"
  }
}
